HO Inventory Planning Dashboard

This dashboard ensures HO always maintains 45-day stock coverage and highlights products that require replenishment from Central or purchase from supplier.”

🎯 Purpose of the Dashboard

This dashboard helps HO store decide:

Which products need replenishment

How much quantity to request from Central Warehouse

Whether Central has enough stock

If Central needs to purchase from supplier

It is a 2-level inventory planning system.

📊 What Data We Used

From your shared files:

1️⃣ Stock Summary File (Oct 1 – Nov 30)

We used:

Sales Out Qty

Other Out Qty

Closing Qty

For HO store only.

2️⃣ Central Warehouse Stock

From stock snapshot:

Current closing stock at Central Warehouse

🧮 Core Business Logic Explained (Non-Technical)

For each product:

Step 1️⃣ — Calculate Daily Consumption

We calculate:

Total Sales in 61 days ÷ 61


This gives:

👉 Average Daily Sales

Step 2️⃣ — Calculate Future Requirement

We project:

Average Daily Sales × 45 days


This gives:

👉 Expected demand for next 45 days

Step 3️⃣ — Calculate Reorder Quantity (HO Level)

We compare:

45-day Requirement − Current HO Stock


If result is positive:

👉 HO needs to request that quantity from Central.

If result is zero or negative:

👉 No order required.